    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the July 6 slate with a lineup optimized for high-ceiling run production against a mix of vulnerable starters. **Yordan Alvarez** (82.97) stands as the premier play, benefiting from a highly favorable matchup against Mikolas (xERA 4.59) and the advantage of hitting second, where his elite 0.484 xwOBA is primed to capitalize on base-running traffic. Joining him in the \"Strong\" tier are **Kyle Schwarber** (70.49) and **Trea Turner** (69.83), who both leverage significant platoon advantages against the lefty Cameron. While **Trea Turner** faces a slightly tougher environment regarding the opponent's ability to hold runners, his lead-off spot remains the engine of our offensive efficiency, and **Kyle Schwarber** continues to demonstrate high-floor utility in the DH slot.\n\nPlatoon edges remain the primary driver for our mid-tier scoring today. **Christian Yelich** (64.83) sees a 13% boost from his favorable matchup against May, maintaining a solid profile despite the presence of a pitcher who manages runners well. Similarly, **Carson Benge** (60.60) cracks the 60+ threshold thanks to a soft matchup against L\u00f3pez, maximizing his value in the five-hole. We are exercising caution with **Junior Caminero** (49.83) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (49.43); both face pitchers with sub-4.00 xERAs, dampening their raw output. **Junior Caminero** in particular faces a tough test against Schlittler, making him a marginal start despite his underlying 0.377 xwOBA. Our bench remains stagnant today, as **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Colt Keith**, and the currently optioned **Hyeseong Kim** are unavailable, leaving us no viable pivot options to challenge the active starters for their slots.",
